### Release GetIconInfo bitmap copies (1/3)

**Severity:** `high`

`GetIconInfo` creates caller-owned mask and color bitmaps, but `ReadIcon` never deletes those copies. Repeated icon reads therefore leak GDI objects, including when `ReadBitmap` returns null; releasing the INFO buffer and extracted icons does not release these bitmaps. Delete both nonzero bitmap handles in the outer `finally`, after pixel conversion. Apply all three suggestions together so the handles and native declaration are available to this cleanup.

```suggestion
                if (mask != IntPtr.Zero)
                {
                    _ = DeleteObject(mask);
                }

                if (color != IntPtr.Zero)
                {
                    _ = DeleteObject(color);
                }

                // The handles of the drawings of the icon belong to the caller, so they have to be given back.
```

### Keep bitmap handles available for cleanup (2/3)

**Severity:** `high`

The mask and color handles are declared inside the `try`, so its corresponding `finally` cannot release them. Move their zero-initialized declarations outside the `try` while retaining the existing icon selection and guard. This allows the companion cleanup to run on successful, null-result and exception exits without changing the icon pixels. Apply all three suggestions together.

```suggestion
            var mask = IntPtr.Zero;
            var color = IntPtr.Zero;

            try
            {
                var icon = large != IntPtr.Zero ? large : small;
                if (icon == IntPtr.Zero)
                {
                    return null;
                }
```
